;;; A pair one of whose sides is concluded through a `forall`: the core leaves
;;; out the facts the universal read, and names none of the commitment —
;;; M1e2 **W21**, register row `W21/forall-core-elim`
;;; (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), banked by S1e2.2.21 (2026-11-05), found
;;; measuring W21's fix (Q-M1e2.15).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program states `(not (in a s2))`. `elim` concludes `(in ?x ?t)` when
;;; every other slot excludes `?x`, through `(forall ?s (and (slot ?s) (neq
;;; ?s ?t)) (not (in ?x ?s)))`, the stdlib's elimination shape: root derives
;;; `(in a s1)` from the stated exclusion. Two candidates, `(tag s1)` and
;;; `(tag s2)`; `(tag s1)` excludes `a` from `s1`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; R is ∅ and {(tag s2)}, and N is {(tag s1)}: committed, `(tag s1)` derives
;;; `(not (in a s1))` against root's `(in a s1)`, a pair, and `elim` derives
;;; `(in a s2)` from it against the stated `(not (in a s2))`, a second. Each
;;; pair rests on both its sides, and `elim`'s side on the exclusion its
;;; universal read: the first rests on `(item a) (slot s1) (not (in a s2))`
;;; and `(tag s1)`, the second on `(item a) (slot s2) (not (in a s2))` and
;;; `(tag s1)`. The core is the smaller in the engine's order, `(item a) (not
;;; (in a s2)) (slot s1) (tag s1)`, which names the commitment.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what holds since ─────────────────────
;;;
;;; Until S1e2.2.21, N's core `(item a) (slot s1)`, by `(given)` and `elim`,
;;; the first pair's positive side without what its universal read
;;; (`ein solve FILE --dump-answer DIR` at `a98a94e3`, release and debug).
;;; With a pair's two sides explained together and nothing more, `(item a)
;;; (not (in a s2)) (slot s2)`: the second pair, its `elim` side again
;;; without what it read, and still no commitment. Since S1e2.2.21's fix, on
;;; the user's ruling of 2026-11-05 on Q-M1e2.15 (b), `(item a) (not (in a
;;; s2)) (slot s1) (tag s1)`, in either build.

(import std.macro :symbols (forall))

(relation item T) (relation slot T) (relation in T T) (relation tag T)

(item a) (slot s1) (slot s2)
(not (in a s2))

(hrule g () :match (slot ?s) :assert (tag ?s))

(rule ex () :match (and (item ?x) (tag ?s)) :assert (not (in ?x ?s)))

(rule elim () :match (and (item ?x) (slot ?t)
                         (forall ?s (and (slot ?s) (neq ?s ?t)) (not (in ?x ?s))))
  :assert (in ?x ?t))
